5494 0 obj
  << /ActualText (I went into these activities mainly wanting to try the different tools and see what interested me\056 Since we were following examples provided in class\054 I wasn\047t creating the designs from scratch\054 but working through them gave me ideas about other ways the technology could be used\056 I didn\047t have a specific project in mind at the beginning\056\nArduino and ProtoPie helped me understand how physical inputs could be read and used in different programs\056 TouchDesigner stood out the most because I enjoyed seeing the inputs affect something visual\056 It was frustrating when the lab computer wouldn\047t run the software\054 but continuing the activity at home gave me more time to explore it\056 I realized I was more interested in creating an interactive visual experience than building a traditional interface\056\nAfter looking into different project ideas\054 I started leaning toward Still Here\056 I like the idea of a space responding to someone simply being there\054 without requiring them to press anything or make a specific gesture\056 I\047m still figuring out which sensor would work best and whether the visual changes would be noticeable enough\056 I think testing those things will help me understand what works and what I might need to change\056 These activities helped me find a direction I\047m interested in exploring further\054 even though the concept is still developing)
     /K [ 7 ]
     /P 5495 0 R
     /Pg 4896 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

