5512 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Still Here asks whether standing in one place can count as an interaction\056 In the proposed installation\054 a wall projection starts yellow and slowly shifts toward orange and red while someone stays in a marked area\056 When they leave\054 the image fades back\056 Most interfaces ask people to tap\054 swipe or move\073 I want to see what happens when simply staying changes the space\056 I like the idea of the room acknowledging someone without taking their picture or storing anything about them\056\015I want the response to feel gradual\054 but not so subtle that someone mistakes it for a video playing on a loop\056 The artwork should be open to \015\ninterpretation\054 with enough feedback for a visitor to recognize that they caused the change\056 I am choosing the Art Path because the question of \015presence interests me more than building a conventional interface)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 5513 0 R
     /Pg 5247 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

